# Build outputs. Each module is compiled from source by the operator against THEIR server, so a
# committed binary would be both useless to them (wrong nginx version, wrong flags, wrong arch)
# and a liability to us: a .so in a public repo is an artifact nobody can reproduce from the tree
# and nobody signed. The three build.sh scripts produce these; the gates consume them.
*.so
*.lo
*.la
*.slo
*.o
.libs/
# The LSIAPI header is fetched from a pinned release rather than vendored, because OpenLiteSpeed is
# GPLv3 and this subtree is MIT. `make litespeed-sdk` puts it here.
litespeed/sdk/
# Gate scratch space and the compiled test drivers. `make -C core check` and the race driver are
# built on demand; test_core and race_core are 1,900 and 474 lines of source each, and the binary
# is of no use to anybody who did not just compile it.
.testtmp/
core/test_core
core/race_core
core/whisper-edge-summary
core/whisper-edge-lookup
